# scripts/proprietary-terms.local.txt  — LOCAL, GITIGNORED
#
# Copy this file to  scripts/proprietary-terms.local.txt  and add the real names that must
# never appear in this public repository: employer / client company names, internal product
# brands, self-hosted service hostnames, internal DB schema names, and so on.
#
# The real file is gitignored on purpose. It restores full-strength scanning on the author's
# machine and in a trusted CI (mount it as a secret file) without ever publishing the names.
# An outside contributor who clones the repo simply runs the structural rules only.
#
# FORMAT
#   - one JavaScript regular expression per line (matched case-insensitively)
#   - blank lines and lines starting with `#` are ignored
#   - `\b` word boundaries and `\s?` optional spaces are useful for name variants
#
# EXAMPLES (these are placeholders — replace with the actual strings)
#   \bacme\s?corp\b
#   \bwidgetpay\b
#   \bgitlab\.acme\b
#   \bacme\.co\.[a-z]{2}\b
#   \binternalproductname\b
